# Open in VS Code with REST Client and use Send Request above each request.
# Run top to bottom. The named POST requests supply the IDs for later requests.
# To repeat a scenario, start again at its POST to create a fresh claim.
# With the kafka Spring profile active, the same workflow requests publish Kafka events.
# See docs/KAFKA.md for the console consumer, outage test and duplicate replay.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8080/api
@motorClaimant = claimant-1
@propertyClaimant = claimant-2
@motorOfficer = officer-1
@propertyOfficer = officer-2

### Motor 1 — Submit a rear-end collision claim. Expect 201 SUBMITTED.
# @name submitMotor
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorClaimant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MOTOR",
  "market": "MY",
  "incidentDate": "2025-10-14",
  "description": "A car struck the rear bumper while I was stopped at a traffic light.",
  "requestedAmount": "2400.00",
  "currency": "MYR"
}

### Motor 2 — List my claims. Expect 200 and the new motor claim in the list.
GET {{baseUrl}}/claims
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorClaimant}}

### Motor 3 — Find the claim in the officer queue. Expect 200 and the submitted claim.
GET {{baseUrl}}/claims?status=SUBMITTED
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}

### Motor 4 — Try reading as another claimant. Expect 404.
GET {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}
X-Demo-User-Id: {{propertyClaimant}}

### Motor 5 — Pick up the claim. Expect 200 UNDER_REVIEW, assigned to officer-1.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"PICK_UP"}

### Motor 6 — Filter the officer's workload. Expect 200 and the motor claim.
GET {{baseUrl}}/claims?status=UNDER_REVIEW&officerId={{motorOfficer}}
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}

### Motor 7 — Try picking up the same claim again as a second officer. Expect 409.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{propertyOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"PICK_UP"}

### Motor 8 — Try asking for information as the unassigned officer. Expect 403.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{propertyOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"REQUEST_INFO","message":"What does the repair estimate cover?"}

### Motor 9 — Request supporting details as the assigned officer. Expect 200 INFO_REQUIRED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"REQUEST_INFO","message":"Please provide the repair estimate breakdown."}

### Motor 10 — Read the officer's question as the claimant. Expect 200 INFO_REQUIRED.
GET {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorClaimant}}

### Motor 11 — Reply with the estimate details. Expect 200 INFO_RECEIVED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorClaimant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"SUPPLY_INFO","message":"The workshop quoted MYR 1600 for parts and MYR 800 for labour."}

### Motor 12 — Resume the review. Expect 200 UNDER_REVIEW.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"RESUME_REVIEW"}

### Motor 13 — Try approving more than requested. Expect 400. The claim remains UNDER_REVIEW.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"APPROVE","approvedAmount":"2500.00","message":"Assessment complete."}

### Motor 14 — Approve the covered repairs. Expect 200 APPROVED with approvedAmount "2200".
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"APPROVE","approvedAmount":"2200.00","message":"Approved the covered parts and labour after applying the MYR 200 excess."}

### Motor 15 — Read the decision as the claimant. Expect 200 APPROVED with the reason in history.
GET {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorClaimant}}

### Motor 16 — Record settlement. Expect 200 SETTLED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"SETTLE"}

### Motor 17 — Check the final status and history. Expect 200 SETTLED and seven entries.
GET {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitMotor.response.body.$.id}}
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorClaimant}}

### Property 1 — Submit a water damage claim. Expect 201 SUBMITTED.
# @name submitProperty
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims
X-Demo-User-Id: {{propertyClaimant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "PROPERTY",
  "market": "SG",
  "incidentDate": "2025-11-03",
  "description": "A gradual leak from a kitchen pipe damaged the lower cabinets.",
  "requestedAmount": "1800.00",
  "currency": "SGD"
}

### Property 2 — Pick up the claim. Expect 200 UNDER_REVIEW, assigned to officer-2.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitProperty.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{propertyOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"PICK_UP"}

### Property 3 — Record a rejection. Expect 200 REJECTED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitProperty.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{propertyOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"REJECT","message":"The demo policy excludes damage from gradual leakage."}

### Property 4 — Read the rejection as the claimant. Expect 200 REJECTED with the reason in history.
GET {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitProperty.response.body.$.id}}
X-Demo-User-Id: {{propertyClaimant}}

### Property 5 — Try settling a rejected claim. Expect 409.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitProperty.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{propertyOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"SETTLE"}

### Dashboard 1 — Add an outstanding SGD claim. Expect 201 SUBMITTED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims
X-Demo-User-Id: {{propertyClaimant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "PROPERTY",
  "market": "SG",
  "incidentDate": "2025-11-04",
  "description": "A storm damaged the roof covering.",
  "requestedAmount": "850.50",
  "currency": "SGD"
}

### Dashboard 2 — Read the team's current workload, estimated exposure and all-time performance. Expect 200.
# On a fresh database after all preceding scenarios, expect 3 total, 1 active,
# 1 unassigned, 2 completed, exposure SGD 850.5, and one of each performance outcome.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}

### Dashboard 3 — Filter historical performance to an earlier UTC period. Expect 200.
# With the examples run today, performance counts are zero and the current snapshot is unchanged.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard?from=2025-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2025-02-01T00:00:00Z
X-Demo-User-Id: {{propertyOfficer}}

### Dashboard 4 — Supply only one date boundary. Expect 400.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard?from=2025-01-01T00:00:00Z
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}

### Dashboard 5 — Try reading the staff dashboard as a claimant. Expect 403.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorClaimant}}

# Start Kafka and run Spring Boot with the kafka profile before this scenario.
# In the Kafka console consumer, look for the claim ID returned by Kafka 1 as the message key.
# For an outage test, stop Kafka, send Kafka 1 and 2, then restart Kafka.
# Both REST requests should succeed during the outage and publish in order after restart.

### Kafka 1 — Submit a fresh claim. Expect 201 and CLAIM_SUBMITTED (sequence 1).
# @name submitKafkaDemo
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorClaimant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MOTOR",
  "market": "MY",
  "incidentDate": "2025-11-05",
  "description": "A parking lot collision damaged the front bumper.",
  "requestedAmount": "750.00",
  "currency": "MYR"
}

### Kafka 2 — Assign the claim. Expect 200 and CLAIM_ASSIGNED (sequence 2).
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitKafkaDemo.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"PICK_UP"}

### Kafka 3 — Try to settle before approval. Expect 409 and no new event.
POST {{baseUrl}}/claims/{{submitKafkaDemo.response.body.$.id}}/actions
X-Demo-User-Id: {{motorOfficer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"SETTLE"}
